€The Recursive Mind challenges the commonly held notion that language is what makes us uniquely human. In this compelling book, Michael Corballis argues that what distinguishes us in the animal kingdom is our capacity for recursion: the ability to embed our thoughts within other thoughts.
Evolutionary psychology.
Human evolution.
Brain -- Evolution.
Language and languages -- Origin."„
Evren bir Buyuk Patlamayla mi basladi? Isik bir dalga mi, bir parcacik mii yoksa her ikisi midir? Kuresel isinmanin nedeni biz miyiz? Her Seyin Teorisi olanakli midir? Bilim icinde yasadigimiz dunyayi ve otesindeki cokli evrenleri anlamamizi olanakli kilmakla, teknolojik ilerlemeler sunmakta ve bilginin sinirlarini genisletmektedir.
Sade bir dille yazilmis olan Bilim Kitabi, kolayca anlasilan kisa ve ozlu aciklamalari, temel ilkelerin dugumlerini adim adim cozen semalari, bilimsel kesifleri unutulmaz kilan klasik alintilari ve bilim anlayisimizi alt ust eden esprili cizimleriyle basucu kitabiniz olacak. Bilgi duzeyiniz ne olursa olsun, ister hevesli bir ogrenci ister konunun teorisyeni olun, bu kitapta sizi kiskirtip canlandiracak cok sey bulacaksiniz.
Katkida Bulunanlar: Adam Hart-Davis, John Farndon, Dan Green, Derek Harvey, Penny Johnson, Douglas Palmer, Steve Parker, Giles Sparrow"’
Edgerton challenges the notion that primitive societies were happy and healthy before they were corrupted and oppressed by colonialism. He surveys a range of ethnographic writings, and shows that many of these so-called innocent societies were cruel, confused and misled."”	
‘	Uzay kac boyutlu? Eger alisageldigimiz 3 uzay boyutunun otesinde baska boyutlar varsa bu fizikte henuz cevaplanmamis pek cok sorunun anahtari olacak. Coklu evrenlerden kara deliklerin iclerine, zaman yolculugundan Buyuk Patlama oncesine kadar bir cok gizemi aydinlatacak. Lisa Randall, dunyanin en heyecan verici bilim yazarlarindan biri ve arastirmasi evrenin tamamen yeni bir bakisinin on cephesinde yer almakta. Bu kitabinda tecrubelerini dunyanin nasil bizim hayal gucumuzun cok daha otesinde olan, gizli ek boyutlarla dolu oldugunu ortaya cikarmak icin kullaniyor: tamamiyla yeni bir gerceklige bir gecit acacak bir gelisme.
"Fizikcilerin, fiziksel gercekligin dogasini aciklamak icin kullandiklari garip ve guclu yeni fikirlerin kolay anlasilir bir aciklamasi."
-Steven Pinker
"Kahramani, Alis Harikalar Diyarinda gibi, Lisa Randall alternatif evrenler hakkinda her seyi biliyor. Alis'in aksine, onlarin nasil calistiklarini aciklamakta oldukca iyi."
- Financial Times
"Karmasik fikirleri basit bir dille aciklamak gibi gerceklestirilmesi neredeyse imkansiz bir beceriyi sergiliyor"
-Daily Express
"Burada mucizeler ve gizemler var"
-The Times Literary Supplement"—

”
How language evolved has been called "the hardest problem in science." In Adam's Tongue, Derek Bickerton--long a leading authority in this field--shows how and why previous attempts to solve that problem have fallen short. Taking cues from topics as diverse as the foraging strategies of ants, the distribution of large prehistoric herbivores, and the construction of ecological niches, Bickerton produces a dazzling new alternative to the conventional wisdom. Language is unique to humans, but it isn't the only thing that sets us apart from other species--our cognitive powers are qualitatively different. So could there be two separate discontinuities between humans and the rest of nature? No, says Bickerton; he shows how the mere possession of symbolic units--words--automatically opened a new and different cognitive universe, one that yielded novel innovations ranging from barbed arrowheads to the Apollo spacecraft. Written in Bickerton's lucid and irreverent style, this book is the first that thoroughly integrates the story of how language evolved with the story of how humans evolved. Sure to be controversial, it will make indispensable reading both for experts in the field and for every reader who has ever wondered how a species as remarkable as ours could have come into existence."¦

